CHAPTER 1: INTRODUCTION
1.1 Introduction
When students or beginners want to get a job in tech — Web Development, Data Analytics, or Android App Development — they routinely get lost. Common questions go unanswered: “Where do I start?”, “What do I learn first?”, “I already know HTML/CSS, why do courses force me to start from zero again?”, and “How many hours will it take to finish?” Generic video courses treat every learner identically, regardless of what they already know, which wastes time and causes many learners to abandon their studies before reaching a job-ready skill set.
PathForge is a Personalized Career Roadmap & Skill Diagnostic Engine built by Mohammad Tameem Mustafa (Roll No. 137) to solve exactly this problem. Instead of giving every learner the same long, boring video course, PathForge benchmarks what the student already knows through a diagnostic quiz and interactive check matrix, pre-credits existing skills so the learner does not waste time relearning them, and generates an ordered, milestone-by-milestone roadmap tailored to the student’s exact career goal. The system also tracks the student’s velocity, study hours, active streaks and project deliverables along the way.
