CHAPTER 2: SOFTWARE REQUIREMENT SPECIFICATION AND PROPOSED SYSTEM
2.1 Proposed System
PathForge is designed as a single-page application centred around one core idea: don’t teach a student what they already know. When a student opens the app, they choose one of five career tracks, then complete a short diagnostic quiz and check matrix. The Roadmap Engine immediately pre-credits any skill the student has already demonstrated and generates a personalised, ordered roadmap covering only the remaining milestones.
The roadmap can then be explored in three complementary views — a visual Timeline/Network, a hands-on IDE Workbench, and a drag-and-drop Kanban board — while a Sprint Planner lets the student trade off pace against graduation date, and a Pomodoro timer supports focused study sessions. An Analytics Dashboard keeps the student motivated with a live progress ring, hours tracker and streak counter.
