DRAWBACKS AND LIMITATIONS PROPOSED
1.	Local storage only. Progress is saved in the browser’s localStorage. Clearing browser history, or opening the app on another device, resets all saved skills and progress.
2.	Mock data. Career tracks, quiz questions and milestones come from a predefined local data file (seedData.ts), not a live cloud server.
3.	No social login. There is currently no “Sign in with Google” or “Sign in with GitHub” option, so there is no real user account system.
4.	No cross-device sync. Because there is no backend, a student’s progress cannot follow them between a phone and a laptop.
