C. How the app works – in simple words
1.	A student opens PathForge and lands on the Career Track Explorer, browsing 5 tracks with duration and salary info.
2.	They pick a track and take the 5-question diagnostic quiz, or use a one-click preset if they want a faster start.
3.	The Roadmap Engine checks each milestone’s required skill against what the diagnostic confirmed — anything already known gets pre-credited and skipped.
4.	The remaining milestones become the student’s personalised roadmap, viewable as a Timeline, an IDE Workbench, or a Kanban board.
5.	Moving the Pace Slider (5–40 hrs/week) instantly recalculates the estimated graduation date, by dividing remaining hours by the chosen pace.
6.	Dragging a Kanban card to Mastered updates that milestone’s status, which immediately updates the Analytics Dashboard’s progress ring and hours count.
7.	The Pomodoro timer runs independently as a 25-minute focus session while the student works through the IDE Workbench.
8.	All of this — track choice, quiz results, Kanban status, theme — is saved to the browser’s localStorage so it survives a page refresh.
